## Import

Import is supported using the following syntax:

```shell
terraform import alkira_service_pan.example SERVICE_ID
```

### Import Behavior

Credential fields (`pan_username`, `pan_password`, `registration_pin_id`,
`registration_pin_value`, `master_key`, `auth_key`, `auth_code`) are
**not returned by the API**. After import, these fields will be empty in
state and `terraform plan` will show a diff for each one.

This is expected. Run `terraform apply` once after import to reconcile
state with your configuration. The apply will update the PAN service
credential (`pan_username`, `pan_password`, `pan_license_key`) in the
Alkira credentials vault. Registration and master key credentials retain
the values set at creation time and are not updated on apply.
Subsequent plans will show no changes.

For `pan_username`, use `admin` for AWS/GCP CXPs or `akadmin` for Azure CXPs.

~> **Note:** Expiry fields (`registration_pin_expiry`, `master_key_expiry`,
`auth_expiry`) are also not returned by the API. If your configuration
includes these, they will show as additions on the first plan after import.
